statement:
Let B be a finite simple 2-connected graph with cyclomatic number
|E(B)|-|V(B)|+1=3. Suppress every maximal path whose internal vertices
have degree two. The resulting loopless 2-connected multigraph K is
isomorphic to exactly one of:
1. two vertices joined by four parallel edges (Q4);
2. a three-vertex triangle with edge multiplicities 2,2,1 (T221);
3. a four-cycle with two opposite edges doubled (D22);
4. the simple graph K4.

Every finite tree-absorbed 2-connected fiber-coherence block of cycle
rank three is exactly one of four relation mechanisms:
1. Q4 four-way intersection;
2. T221 ternary join after two parallel intersections;
3. D22 cycle monodromy after two parallel intersections;
4. a four-variable K4 binary CSP.
There is no fifth branch-kernel mechanism at cycle rank three.

For the six inequality blocks of the three-color K4 core:
1. deleting one block gives exactly 6 solutions;
2. deleting two adjacent K4 edges gives exactly 12 solutions;
3. deleting two disjoint K4 edges gives exactly 18 solutions.

For the q-color K_(q+1) core of R3K04:
1. every one-edge deletion has q! solutions;
2. two adjacent edge deletions have 2q! solutions;
3. two disjoint edge deletions have 3q! solutions;
4. N_1=binom(q+1,2)q! and
   N_2=3 binom(q+1,4)q!.
